    {
      "entry_id": "bitmap-import-linear",
      "subject": "16-bit bitmap source on RGB16, sRGB8, RGB8 and L16 channels",
      "status": "exact",
      "formula": "A bitmap code c of an n-bit image is taken as the linear value float32(c / (2^n - 1)) whatever the colour-space tag (untagged PNG 16 here) and stored with the channel's write rule: RGB16/L16 the code itself, RGB8 the 8-bit write rule, sRGB8 the GPU float-to-sRGB8 conversion (entry uniform-colour-srgb8-store). A grey bitmap feeds the grey channel. Bound by the SHA-256 of the file bytes, decoded once per resource.",
      "public_sources": [
        {
          "source_id": "X-D3D12",
          "locator": "Data conversion rules: FLOAT to UNORM, UNORM to FLOAT"
