    {
      "entry_id": "bitmap-height-signed",
      "subject": "Bitmap source on the Height channel",
      "status": "exact",
      "formula": "On the Height channel a bitmap value t = float32(c / 65535) is stored as float32(float32(2 t) - 1), written to the channel's L16F storage toward zero; the OpenEXR export holds it unchanged. The Height channel is signed with base 0 (every template), so a fill at opacity a stores a (2 t - 1); its 16-bit PNG export is the write rule of (h + 1) / 2 (the empty channel's code 32767). A second fill in LinearDodge doubles it.",
      "public_sources": [
        {
          "source_id": "X-D3D12",
          "locator": "Data conversion rules: FLOAT to UNORM, UNORM to FLOAT"
        },
